// A high lower-staff chord (C5-E5-G5, on ledger lines that reach the UPPER staff's
// bottom line) must widen the inter-staff gap so the chord and its ledgers clear
// those LINES, not just the upper staff's notes. LilyPond's per-staff spacing skyline
// includes the staff symbol, so a neighbour's notes clear the staff lines themselves.
// Guards SkylineBuilder.SeedStaffSymbol.
//
// Measured 2026-08-16 (bottom line of the upper staff -> top line of the lower):
//   chord      Lily#    LilyPond 2.26.0
//   C3-E3-G3   5.000    5.000     <- the FLOOR: nothing about skylines is measured
//   C4-E4-G4   5.000    5.000     <- still the floor
//   C5-E5-G5   8.090    8.095     <- opens; the 0.005 is the SVG's 2-decimal rounding
// and with SeedStaffSymbol disabled, ONLY the C5 spelling's picture moves.
//
// ⚠️ Do not "correct" this chord downwards. It read <c e g> (C3-E3-G3) until 2026-08-16
// while this header claimed C4-E4-G4, so the book defended nothing for as long as it
// existed — and the claimed C4-E4-G4 would ALSO have defended nothing, because a bass
// staff's G4 still sits below the upper staff's bottom line at this gap. Reaching the
// upper staff's PITCH RANGE and reaching its LINES are different things; only the second
// makes the seed binding.
//
// ⚠️ The upper staff climbs an octave between the bars (c'1 | c'1 in relative octaves is
// C5 then C6). Left as written: measured, the gap is identical for every lower-chord
// spelling above, so nothing here reads it.
title "Inter-staff: high bass chord"
time 4/4
key c major

part rh { clef treble }
part lh { clef bass }

section Main {
  rh { c'1 | c'1 | }
  lh { c4 d e f | <c'' e'' g''>1 | }
}

form main { Main }

score main "grandstaff-high-bass" {
  staff rh
  staff lh
}
